</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE VII: </span>Failure Projector Architecture</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S8.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation. </span> We provide a qualitative evaluation of the raw world model latent space of Dreamer in the Dubins Car. Fig. <a href="#S8.F9" title="Fig. 9 ‣ VIII-B Failure Projector ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows both the feature similarities computed using unprojected world model latents and the corresponding safety value function learned with these latents. Compared to the results learned from projected features shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ V-A Experimental Setup ‣ V Simulation Results ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ V-B Can AnySafe Adapt to Diverse Safety Constraints? ‣ V Simulation Results ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the unprojected similarities fail to represent position-based, failure-relevant distinctions, resulting in poorly learned value functions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S8.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.19555v1/raw_dreamer.png" id="S8.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/128;" width="476" height="128" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 9: </span><span id="S8.F9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dubins’ Car Qualitative Result with Raw Unprojected Features.</span> We visualize the latent similarity and safety value function at heading slices <math id="S8.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\{0,\pi/4,\pi/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\{0,\pi/4,\pi/2\}</annotation></semantics></math> using the raw Dreamer features without applying the failure projector.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-C</span> </span><span id="S8.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Calibration of Latent Similarity</span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Sec. <a href="#S4" title="IV Constraint-Parameterized Latent Safety Filter ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>, we compute a threshold for defining a latent failure set and then apply this threshold at runtime for safety filtering in (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In IV Constraint-Parameterized Latent Safety Filter ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), operating on the safety value function. Formally, this calibration procedure guarantees only that the similarity measure—and the corresponding failure set—are calibrated. Approximate value function solvers (e.g, RL) can still induce errors in the downstream safety filter, and calibrating the value function directly requires stronger assumptions about access to the ground-truth unsafe set labels <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. Nevertheless, we prove in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ VIII-C Calibration of Latent Similarity ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ AnySafe: Adapting Latent Safety Filters at Runtime via Safety Constraint Parameterization in the Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> that under a perfect value function solver, the calibrated threshold <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> can be applied directly to the value function learned from the similarity measure, yielding an unsafe set defined as the sub-threshold level set of the value function.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, we show that learning a threshold-dependent safety value function <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> with a safety margin <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}^{\delta}:=\ell_{z}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}^{\delta}:=\ell_{z}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, is equivalent to learning the value function <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the raw latent similarity <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying the threshold <math id="S8.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> post hoc. This equivalence implies that calibration can be performed after computing the value function using the latent similarities without adjusting them with thresholds, whereas threshold-dependent training would require recomputing the value function whenever the threshold changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a safety margin function. Consider the discrete-time safety Bellman backup operator:</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(TV)(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(TV)(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,\ell(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,\ell(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\gamma\min\Big\{\ell(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{z}_{t+1}\sim f_{z}(\cdot\mid z_{t},a_{t})}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\gamma\min\Big\{\ell(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{z}_{t+1}\sim f_{z}(\cdot\mid z_{t},a_{t})}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its unique fixed point. For a constant <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}^{\delta}:=\ell_{z}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}^{\delta}:=\ell_{z}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> be the safety Bellman backup operator <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> where the margin function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}^{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}^{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(T_{\delta}V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T_{\delta}V)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(z_{t})=(1-\gamma)\,(\ell(z_{t})-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(z_{t})=(1-\gamma)\,(\ell(z_{t})-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\gamma\min\Big\{\ell(z_{t})-\delta,\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{z}_{t+1}\sim f_{z}(\cdot\mid z_{t},a_{t})}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\gamma\min\Big\{\ell(z_{t})-\delta,\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{z}_{t+1}\sim f_{z}(\cdot\mid z_{t},a_{t})}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the fixed point of this Bellman backup be <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}\;=\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}\;=\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{\,z:\;V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}(z)&lt;0\,\}\;=\;\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)&lt;\delta\,\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{\,z:\;V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}(z)&lt;0\,\}\;=\;\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)&lt;\delta\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:\mathcal{Z}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:\mathcal{Z}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be any value function. Recall the linearity of expectation and the shift-invariance identities:</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min\{a-\delta,b-\delta\}\;=\;\min\{a,b\}-\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\{a-\delta,b-\delta\}\;=\;\min\{a,b\}-\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{a-\delta,b-\delta\}\;=\;\max\{a,b\}-\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{a-\delta,b-\delta\}\;=\;\max\{a,b\}-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{z}^{\delta}=\ell_{z}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{z}^{\delta}=\ell_{z}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(T_{\delta}(V-\delta))(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T_{\delta}(V-\delta))(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,(\ell_{z}(z_{t})-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,(\ell_{z}(z_{t})-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t})-\delta,\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[\,V(\hat{z}_{t+1})-\delta\,\big]\Big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t})-\delta,\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[\,V(\hat{z}_{t+1})-\delta\,\big]\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,\ell_{z}(z_{t})-(1-\gamma)\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\,\ell_{z}(z_{t})-(1-\gamma)\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma\Big(\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}-\delta\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma\Big(\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}-\delta\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big((1-\gamma)\,\ell_{z}(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big((1-\gamma)\,\ell_{z}(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}\Big)-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma\min\!\Big\{\ell_{z}(z_{t}),\;\max_{a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbb{E}\big[V(\hat{z}_{t+1})\big]\Big\}\Big)-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(TV)(z_{t})-\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(TV)(z_{t})-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, if <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fixed point of <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, then,</span></p>
<table id="S8.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\delta}({V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta)=T{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\delta}({V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta)=T{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed point of <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the fixed point is unique <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}={V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the corresponding unsafe sets are equivalent:</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{\,z:\;V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}(z)&lt;0\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{\,z:\;V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}_{\delta}(z)&lt;0\,\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)-\delta&lt;0\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)-\delta&lt;0\,\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)&lt;\delta\,\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext class="fas fa-shield-alt">
<span class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-shield-alt">
</span></mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\,z:\;{V^{\text{\tiny{\faIcon[*]{shield-alt}}}}}(z)&lt;\delta\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
